# Cloudflare Pages security headers for Dark Flags
#
# Dark Flags measures which browser features are exposed, so a restrictive
# Permissions-Policy would corrupt its own readings; there is none. The CSP is
# real, though: the page's one inline script is authorised by its hash (not by
# 'unsafe-inline'), so an injected event handler or script never runs even if
# a third-party API response reached innerHTML. Anything the probes need is
# allowed explicitly: cross-site images for the login check, data: for canvas
# thumbnails, the three IP-intelligence APIs,
# 'wasm-unsafe-eval' for the WebAssembly probe, and Cloudflare Web Analytics,
# which the Pages host injects at the edge (script from static.cloudflareinsights.com,
# beacon to cloudflareinsights.com). STUN is not governed by CSP.
# Inline style attributes are used for the comparison bars; style injection
# cannot run code, so style-src keeps 'unsafe-inline'.
#
# THE HASH MUST MATCH index.html BYTE FOR BYTE. After editing index.html run
#   node tools/csp-hash.mjs <dir>
# before deploying, or the browser refuses the app's own script.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com 'sha256-rkHnH/sKb5HD9gN+tABrFZhIBTXmLLQ3XMcsCKhIcsk=' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; img-src * data: blob:; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com https://ipwho.is https://get.geojs.io https://api.ipapi.is; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; media-src 'self' data: blob:; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
